Host the Shape Detection API on HarmonyOS ScanKit and CoreVisionKit.

The detectors are new code under overlay/components/ohos_shape_detection/.
They reach the kits through ArkTS, which runs only in the app's main process,
so this patch only changes upstream-owned files:

  * content/browser/shape_detection/shape_detection_service.cc binds the
    service inside the browser process on OHOS instead of asking the GPU
    process, which is a separate process on tablets and cannot reach ArkTS.
  * content/browser/BUILD.gn links //components/ohos_shape_detection.

The three detectors are exposed with --enable-blink-features at startup
(ohos_chrome_main_runner.cc) rather than in runtime_enabled_features.json5,
which would regenerate a header most of Blink includes.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch. Apply
this patch once to a persistent runner whose main adapter patch is already
present:

  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-shape-detection.patch

diff --git a/content/browser/BUILD.gn b/content/browser/BUILD.gn
index b92e284..4a9a49d 100644
--- a/content/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/content/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -2648,6 +2648,12 @@ source_set("browser") {
     ]
   }
 
+  # HarmonyOS hosts the shape detection service in the browser process; see
+  # shape_detection/shape_detection_service.cc.
+  if (is_ohos) {
+    deps += [ "//components/ohos_shape_detection" ]
+  }
+
   if (is_apple) {
     sources += [
       "font_access/font_enumeration_data_source_mac.h",
